function t = central_drift_template()
%CENTRAL_DRIFT_TEMPLATE  Luminance template of one central-drift segment.
%
%   The central-drift pattern is a ring of identical elements. This function
%   returns the luminance of a single element, sampled on a regular grid in the
%   local frame of the element, together with the geometry needed to place
%   copies of it around the ring. The element's luminance runs as a continuous
%   asymmetric gradient from dark to light, and it is that gradient, repeated
%   around the ring, that drives the illusory motion.
%
%   Outputs
%     t  struct with fields:
%        template    39 x 63 double. Luminance of one element, in the same
%                    units as meanL_ref, sampled at the grid points given by
%                    u_centers and v_centers.
%        u_centers   1 x 63 double. Sample positions along the tangential
%                    direction of the ring, in reference pixels.
%        v_centers   1 x 39 double. Sample positions along the radial
%                    direction of the ring, in reference pixels.
%        n_segments  double. Number of elements around the ring.
%        r_mid       double. Radius of the ring, in reference pixels, measured
%                    to the centre of the elements.
%        meanL_ref   double. Background luminance of the template.
%        ref_N       double. Canvas side, in pixels, that r_mid and the sample
%                    positions refer to. Other canvas sizes are handled by
%                    scaling everything by N/ref_N.
%
%   Example
%     t = central_drift_template();
%     imagesc(t.u_centers, t.v_centers, t.template); axis image

t.n_segments = 12;
t.r_mid      = 128.624102358;
t.meanL_ref  = 204;
t.ref_N      = 396;

